{"title":"2004 IMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(<i>Hojoo Lee</i>) Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/e/49e6a2d706867d6652d7edadccc3fd034130bd98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> be an integer. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/7/6f7c2b098cd1b3bcb2106023be91ade438c85d45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_1, t_2, \\dots , t_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"15\" /> be positive real numbers such that \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/6/ba65423b7f49161183ab65b702bf0dadb017ee63.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n^2 + 1 &gt; \\left( t_1 + t_2 + ... + t_n \\right) \\left( \\frac {1}{t_1} + \\frac {1}{t_2} + ... + \\frac {1}{t_n} \\right).\\]\" width=\"386\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/3/273e0046b505d99f3d1167caa82b2ac76c96d075.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/5/a652022db81b0ec1c066b09e32932b7b7e0cd716.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"15\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/f/5df9ff73586b830a77fd20e48c09ec0621c07db8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" /> are side lengths of a triangle for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/5/ab58307d8a20377d430885cf4d2c2c342e910abf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\leq i &lt; j &lt; k \\leq n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/5635737307f5f0651cced8ee2e6558a426fd27b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, suppose (for sake of contradiction) that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/d/38dc222d0b6f9882bc575b2b498a834948c39634.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_3 = t_2 + t_1 + k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"120\" height=\"15\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/7/cb745f62ddf5625f47a60b8976c60faebcf74f43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />; then (by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cauchy-Schwarz_Inequality\" title=\"Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality\">Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality</a>)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/4/2a421058bd1e64a4a0404a6d4049d8a667f401f9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}10 &amp;&gt; [2(t_1 + t_2) + k]\\left(\\frac {1}{t_1} + \\frac {1}{t_2} + \\frac 1{t_1 + t_2 + k}\\right) = 2(t_1+t_2)\\left(\\frac 1{t_1} + \\frac{1}{t_2}\\right) + \\left(\\frac{k}{t_1} + \\frac k{t_2}\\right) + \\frac{2t_1 + 2t_2 + k}{t_1 + t_2 + k}\\\\ &amp;\\ge 8 + \\left(\\frac{k}{t_1} + \\frac k{t_2}\\right) + 2 - \\frac{k}{t_1 + t_2 + k}\\\\ &amp;= 10 + k\\left(\\frac{1}{t_1} + \\frac {1}{t_2} - \\frac{1}{t_1 + t_2+k}\\right) \\ge 10\\end{align*}\" width=\"770\" height=\"142\" />\n</p><p>so it is true for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/5635737307f5f0651cced8ee2e6558a426fd27b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />. We now claim the result by induction; for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/b/d1b94ea0cc3ac2d353695f157196aed47896fefc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, we have \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/a/76a6d3107264b76774a54981b850f8bb4812539c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}f(n) &amp;:= \\left( t_1 + t_2 + ... + t_n \\right) \\left( \\frac {1}{t_1} + \\frac {1}{t_2} + ... + \\frac {1}{t_n} \\right) \\\\ &amp;= \\left( t_1 + t_2 + ... + t_{n-1} \\right) \\left( \\frac {1}{t_1} + \\frac {1}{t_2} + ... + \\frac {1}{t_{n-1}} \\right) + t_n \\sum_{i=1}^{n-1} \\frac 1{t_i} + \\frac{1}{t_n} \\sum_{i=1}^{n-1} t_i + 1\\end{align*}\" width=\"601\" height=\"101\" />\n</p><p>By <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AM-GM\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"AM-GM\">AM-GM</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/a/8bad411d02f94038eb02cccac2d42b4abe88c0af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{t_n}{t_i} + \\frac{t_i}{t_n} \\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"94\" height=\"39\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/1/511974da0373576a26dabf1a4bd228ec85f4ff7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) \\ge f(n-1) + 2(n-1) + 1 = f(n-1) + 2n - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"410\" height=\"18\" />. Then the problem is reduced to proving the statement true for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bdca93962a2beaffc172ca394e04fe05bd74ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> numbers, as desired.<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/3/fa3c25f5564e5b25bbbb72f5b18ce4c5ead52471.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\\square$\" width=\"599\" height=\"12\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the method of Lagrange multipliers. \n</p><p>Suppose WLOG <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/6/c2689a011c3a62b37b1368a3d1af3f6ee4115e85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_1 \\geq \\cdots \\geq t_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/8/de8cde18d7e50aec1a984c8d1fd7809c178515dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_1+\\cdots + t_n = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"130\" height=\"17\" />. We must show all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/1/211a5fc11c48cf06b3b24f6c8b0b720a99c82454.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_i,t_j,t_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> satisfy the triangle equality. For this it suffices to show <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/9/4d9d91fd7870c0978b2cc4eefd787f9d10099ae5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_{n-1}+t_n &gt; t_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"111\" height=\"17\" /> since that is the worst case scenario. Suppose by contradiction <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/f/67f346dcec810196b29abf066c07298cc015968a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_1 \\geq t_n + t_{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"111\" height=\"17\" />. We claim \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c5834113e9da8554598b2782d4afa9e2ab8a830.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{t_1}+\\cdots + \\frac{1}{t_n} \\stackrel{(1)}{\\geq} \\frac{1}{t_1&#39;} + \\frac{1}{t_2} + \\cdots + \\frac{1}{t_{n-1}}+\\frac{1}{t_n&#39;} \\stackrel{(2)}{\\geq} n^2 + 1 \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ (3)\\]\" width=\"456\" height=\"42\" />\nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/9/36900eedfd2ccdb8c22a51b10343b1b449785fcb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_1&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"16\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/8/0186ed606c450d8761187ab9d1ad567b0abde90c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_n&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"17\" height=\"20\" /> are the unique solution to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/c/34c80c0fd55b15cebeb758f2a663004b6ecee5d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_1&#39; = t_{n-1}+t_n&#39;, t_1&#39; + t_n&#39; = t_1 + t_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"247\" height=\"20\" />. To show <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/6/ab6e4e0ead588cf3df72efc390be475ac37b285e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=t_1+t_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"16\" /> and note <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/4/2d40033342234ad4f0308e74f5d85c10fd7f56c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = \\frac{1}{x} + \\frac{1}{c-x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"143\" height=\"40\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/3/a1387afbf8bd8cdf46f5c3efe6c950d2d6aea986.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f&#39;(x) \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"20\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/8/8d896a7bc81e93db2b5befd4c527b523d32588c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\geq c/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"63\" height=\"20\" />. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/0/f7098c3184d5d5d97880bef8b42c98b1cb0ad182.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(t_1) \\geq f(t_1&#39;)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"20\" /> (note <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/2/682cab8532d1c3b8a4d2c63f3d1fd83c329e9037.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_1 \\geq t_1&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"54\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/5/725249e682b45197a1926ad87dd32ae78d8991ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_1&#39; &gt; t_n&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/f/28fdbaf36d48da09bf04e6748394d14944371921.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_1&#39; &gt; c/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"66\" height=\"20\" />). To show <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62f62a19f0425d8e6121ca0c1cfd3ce96e43c9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />, apply the method of Lagrange multipliers to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/8/01884f32deb0f6324c03d56d345d512be24a4eef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{t_{n-1}+t_n&#39;} + \\frac{1}{t_2} + \\cdots + \\frac{1}{t_{n-1}} + \\frac{1}{t_n&#39;}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"261\" height=\"43\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/9/af9100a673648d03d6703816754e69af8a292acf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_{n-1}+t_n&#39; + t_2 + \\cdots + t_{n-1} + t_n&#39; = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"278\" height=\"20\" /> to find the only extremum (which is a minimum since the boundary points are undefined/have the summation go to infinity) \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/a/68a822c8305df81dc3de3571de4a1b12d812e7dc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} t_2&#39; = \\cdots = t_{n-2}&#39; &amp;= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\lambda}} \\\\  t_{n-1} = t_n&#39; &amp;= \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2 \\sqrt{2} \\sqrt{\\lambda}} \\end{align*}\" width=\"202\" height=\"94\" />\nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/d/cbd9069f6ca294974e81d81be230e1a9968e6415.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\lambda} = n-3 + \\sqrt{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"150\" height=\"21\" />. In this case (recall <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/8/a38a8a15c62187543e285bf5fc98d740ebae766e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_1&#39; = t_{n-1} + t_n&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"111\" height=\"20\" />)\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/7/37751e65d2d099246f89e3ff9460b28399237751.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{t_1&#39;}+ \\frac{1}{t_2} + \\cdots + \\frac{1}{t_{n-1}} + \\frac{1}{t_n&#39;} = (n-3+\\sqrt{10})^2\\]\" width=\"342\" height=\"41\" />\nwhich one can easily verify is greater than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/5/0f55a7827b23d850bed0d0c3bf0880b27ffcca2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"16\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/e/49e6a2d706867d6652d7edadccc3fd034130bd98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> (equality holds for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/5635737307f5f0651cced8ee2e6558a426fd27b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />). This shows <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62f62a19f0425d8e6121ca0c1cfd3ce96e43c9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />, hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/8/b88ea3916e8089c7edbccc3ff91e58e01a6e2682.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />, which is a contradiction.\n</p><p>~not_detriti\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>&lt;url&gt;viewtopic.php?p=99756#99756 AoPS/MathLinks discussion&lt;/url&gt;</li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO\" title=\"2004 IMO\">2004 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2004 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2004 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2004 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2004 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2004 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2004 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2004 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2004 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017203900\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.033 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.045 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 295/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 10703/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.912      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.912      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7372:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017203900 and revision id 286495. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}